About The Role

Our client, a Fortune 15 healthcare organization, is seeking a highly motivated Data Analyst for a contract position based in Morris Plains, NJ (hybrid). In this role, you will support teams focused on affordability programs, patient insurance solutions, and business operations. You will play a key part in transforming complex data into actionable insights that influence product strategy, operational decision-making, and executive-level discussions. This is an excellent opportunity for a data professional seeking visibility across both operational and product-focused initiatives, while helping to improve affordability and accessibility for patients. You will collaborate closely with business stakeholders, analyze trends, build dashboards, and support reporting initiatives, all while staying current with emerging analytics and AI capabilities. The position offers mentorship, training on niche technologies, and the chance to make a tangible impact within a leading healthcare company.

What You'll Do

Analyze data related to affordability programs, patient assistance initiatives, and insurance-focused products
Develop and maintain dashboards and reporting solutions using Power BI or Tableau
Write SQL queries to extract, transform, and analyze data from multiple sources
Perform operational reporting and business analysis related to retail channel performance
Partner with business leaders to identify trends, opportunities, and potential risks
Stay informed on emerging analytics and AI capabilities to improve reporting and insight generation
Provide actionable insights to influence product strategy and operational decision-making
Support executive-level discussions with data-driven recommendations

What You Bring

Experience in Data Analytics, Business Analytics, or a related field
Advanced SQL skills with experience querying large datasets
Experience building dashboards and reporting solutions in Tableau or Power BI
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills
Excellent verbal and written communication abilities
Strong interpersonal skills and a collaborative, team-oriented mindset
Experience with Python is a plus

What's In It For You

Opportunity to start your career at a Fortune 15 healthcare company
Mentorship and training from senior technologists
Training on niche technologies such as Hadoop
Weekly paychecks
Onsite cafeteria

